WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.900
- I knew the morning of the 26th

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:05.410
that there was something wrong.

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:06.343
You could feel it.

00:00:09.487 --> 00:00:11.960
(dramatic music)
(fire crackling)

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:14.720
It was just a sea of
fire coming over the hill

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:16.020
burning into the city.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.550
From the hospital you could see almost

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:23.992
the whole entire thing.

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:30.860
- My name is Ed Zawada.

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:34.710
I am a staff physician
at Mercy Medical Center.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.070
I provide care for kidney patients

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.450
and ICU patients.

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:40.060
- My name's Kenneth Luke.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:43.110
I am the Disaster Infectious Diseases

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:45.450
and Base Station Coordinator.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.240
The fire took on a life of its own.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:50.800
- We kept hearing that this
fire was continuing to spread.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.670
This is a city of around 90,000 people.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:56.483
Thirty thousand people were evacuated.

00:00:57.770 --> 00:00:59.930
- [Kenneth] The red area on this map

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:02.210
is the complete burn from the fire

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:04.930
with the winds being so high and so fast

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:06.210
it actually blew embers

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:07.440
over to the other side of the river,

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.910
which was where a majority
of the homes were burned.

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:11.670
- [Nancy] I finally planted those roses

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:12.680
in the front of the house

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:15.000
and after the fire, they were a puddle

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.000
of melted plastic.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.913
That was what was left of our house.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:22.140
- [Ed] I knew there'd be damage

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:23.788
but total destruction?

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:29.360
- [Nancy] People were
surprised that Ed went back

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:31.440
to work the next day.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:33.350
- You can't sit around and mope.

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:35.770
All that's left now is
the present and the future

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:37.317
and that's not a bad thing.

00:01:37.317 --> 00:01:39.260
- [Kenneth] Human kindness was displayed

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:41.480
throughout this whole entire event.

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:43.350
Many, many staff lost their homes

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:45.790
or evacuated and just came to work

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:47.250
because they knew that the patients

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:48.440
still needed to be taken care of.

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:50.600
They knew that the
communities still needed us.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:52.170
- From administration to staff,

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:54.910
they were gonna find a
way to help and they did.

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:57.190
- [Kenneth] We set up an
employee assistance program;

00:01:57.190 --> 00:01:58.670
we had a lot a of counselors come in

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:00.010
and set up regular counseling.

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:03.340
They set up funds to
help reimburse employees

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:04.630
to get them back on their feet.

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:06.050
- [Ed] They made supplies available,

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:07.430
made some support available,

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:08.650
made some money available.

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:10.010
- [Kenneth] Anybody who was evacuated,

00:02:10.010 --> 00:02:11.520
anybody who lost their home,

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:12.780
they helped them out.

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:16.547
- Why are we here if it's
not to help each other?

00:02:16.547 --> 00:02:19.950
Human kindness, I think
is the responsibility

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:22.047
of every person on this planet.

